' diagram-type: sequence
@startuml
title Durable FlowAI task trace correlation

participant Listener
participant "State Registry" as Registry
database PostgreSQL as DB
participant Executor
participant "OpenHands Agent Server" as OpenHands
participant "OTel Collector" as Collector

Listener -> Registry: POST task + traceparent
activate Registry
Registry -> DB: persist pending task
Registry -> Collector: ingestion span
Registry --> Listener: canonical task
deactivate Registry

... durable wait; no span remains open ...

Executor -> Registry: claim + traceparent
activate Registry
Registry -> DB: atomic FIFO claim + created event
Registry -> Collector: claim server span
Registry --> Executor: task + command_id
deactivate Registry

activate Executor
Executor -> Collector: executor.task.run span\n(link to available claim context)
Executor -> OpenHands: POST conversation + traceparent
activate OpenHands
OpenHands -> Collector: conversation / agent.step / LLM / tool spans
OpenHands --> Executor: conversation_id + event stream
deactivate OpenHands
Executor -> Registry: running then terminal events + traceparent
Executor -> Collector: finish executor.task.run
deactivate Executor

note over Executor,OpenHands
If OpenHands starts a separate root, correlate with
task_id, command_id, executor_id, and conversation_id.
end note
@enduml
